    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 011037\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n337 AM PDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Above-normal temperatures and quiet conditions continue into\n  next week as high pressure dominates.\n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through Wednesday.\n\nEnsemble guidances is in good agreement on the development of a \nridge over the southwestern US today and sticking around through at \nleast the middle of next week. This feature will promote anomalously \nwarm temperatures, with forecast highs up to 10 degrees above normal \nat times. However, heat risk during this time largely remains in the \nminor category, with just Death Valley in the moderate to major \ncategories. A weak disturbance passing through on Sunday and Monday \ntries to spur a slight uptick in winds and minor cooling, but \nimpacts are not expected. Precipitation chances stay below 5% across \nthe entire area.\n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Clear \nskies and light winds last through the TAF period. Expect variable \nlight winds to increase slightly and turn easterly by the late \nmorning. These winds reduce into the evening and become variable \nagain. Winds will remain light into Friday morning and become more \nnortheasterly.\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 12Z Forecast Package...Clear skies continue \nacross the region with weaker winds expected. Aside from the \npossibility of a brief stray gust, expect winds speeds to remain \nbelow 10 kts. Wind directions look to be mostly variable during the \novernight hours with some of the more consistent wind directions \ndetermined by local effects and not a widespread prevailing\npattern.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Woods\nAVIATION...Murdock\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
